```

### Why this works

| Concern | How it is addressed |
|---|---|
| **No task on insert** | Only the `TriggerAction.AfterUpdate` interface is implemented; no `AfterInsert` handler is registered. |
| **No task when Amount is unchanged** | `opp.Amount != oldOpp.Amount` comparison (null-safe in Apex). |
| **At most one task per opp per txn despite re-entry** | `static Set<Id> processedIds` — populated on the first (Order 10) execution; the second execution triggered by the Order 20 rounding `update` skips already-seen Ids. The static set lives for the entire transaction and is garbage-collected afterward. |
| **Bulk-safe / single DML** | All qualifying tasks are accumulated in `tasksToInsert` and inserted with **one** `insert` call, comfortably handling 200+ opportunities within DML limits. |
| **Rounding action untouched** | `TA_Opportunity_RoundAmount` (Order 20) is unchanged; our action runs first (Order 10), captures the user-initiated change, and the static set neutralises the phantom second execution. |

