### Recommended wrapper for the 200-opportunity case

Because 200 emails exceeds the 50-per-transaction async limit, the scheduled job should delegate to a `Batchable` class (batch size ≤ 50) whose `execute` method calls `RenewalReminderService.sendReminders`. Example shape (not part of the requested files, just guidance):

```java
global class RenewalReminderBatch implements Database.Batchable<Id>, Database.AllowsCallouts {
    global Iterable<Id> start(Database.BatchableContext bc) { /* query due opps */ }
    global void execute(Database.BatchableContext bc, List<Id> scope) {
        RenewalReminderService.sendReminders(scope);   // scope.size() <= 50
    }
    global void finish(Database.BatchableContext bc) { /* summary */ }
}
```

Schedule it with `Database.executeBatch(new RenewalReminderBatch(), 50)` on Mondays via `CronTrigger`.
